# proto-file: flatsat/hardware/devices.proto
# proto-message: flatsat.v1.ImuDevice
#
# IMU device specification — ONE source of truth for two consumers: the
# flight-side driver reads this to know the device; the simulation's
# sensor model reads THE SAME file to corrupt truth the way this device
# would. Values are placeholder/representative (a consumer MEMS gyro
# class part) until a physical IMU is on the bench.

name: "imu0"
rate_hz: 100

# Gyro
gyro_noise_rad_s: 0.002        # white noise sigma per axis
gyro_full_scale_rad_s: 4.363   # ±250 °/s — saturates (and flags) beyond
gyro_lsb_rad_s: 1.33e-4        # quantization step (16-bit over full scale)

# Accelerometer (published but unused by rate damping)
accel_noise_m_s2: 0.02
accel_full_scale_m_s2: 156.9   # ±16 g

# Housekeeping
temperature_c: 25.0          # initial/nominal die temperature
# Orbital thermal model (designed values until characterization): the die
# relaxes toward these equilibria as the vehicle crosses the terminator.
temperature_sunlit_c: 38.0
temperature_eclipse_c: 4.0
thermal_time_constant_s: 420.0
